## Lore

The Order of the White Rose began as a breakaway from the Mystic Knights, the
feared and evil mercenary order of the Magic Zone. Its members kept the
training - martial and magical combat, P.P.E. channelling, espionage and a hard
edge toward evil - and turned it to protecting the innocent. In practice they
are Mystic Knights of good alignment, which is exactly why some people who
meet them are uneasy.

They still work as mercenaries, but only for good clients, charging those who
can pay and helping the rest for free, and they go out of their way to take
jobs that set them against the Mystic Knights and their supernatural patrons.
The Magic Zone is their chosen battlefield: it was their home, it is the Mystic
Knights'' base, and few other heroes will operate there for long.

The Mystic Knights hunt them relentlessly and publicly deny the Order still
exists. The White Knights hide their faces and names, never lead an enemy home
to their hidden Garden in Madhaven, and raise money through front operations
such as Bethesda Mercenary Enterprises.

## Code of the Order

The Knights swear to protect the innocent and their freedoms, champion justice
and equality, fight evil wherever it appears and whatever the odds, destroy the
Mystic Knights and their masters, pursue enlightenment and nobility, go where
justice is most needed (the Magic Zone and the eastern wilds above all), and
never betray a member or reveal the Garden, even under torture.

## Magic

The Knight''s magic is intuitive. After years of reflection, a three day ordeal
of fasting and meditation (or of constant battle) leaves the character knowing
seven spells: Magic Shield, Armor of Ithan, Aura of Death, Tongues, Energize
Spell, Fist of Fury and Power Weapon. At each later level he meditates and
gains two more from invocation levels 1-6. He is never taught spells and does
not seek them, but happily uses Techno-Wizard devices and prizes magic weapons
and armor, rune weapons above all.

P.P.E. is 2D4x10 plus P.E., +2D6 per level, and the Knight draws twice the
usual amount from ley lines and nexus points.

## Psionics

A major psychic. Starts with See the Invisible, Sixth Sense, Resist Fatigue and
Mind Block, plus three Sensitive or Physical powers of choice. Gains one more
Sensitive or Physical power per level from second, plus one Super power at
fourth level and another at ninth. I.S.P. is 5D6+4 plus M.E., +1D6+1 per level.

## Equipment and Money

Beyond the kit listed in the class, a Knight starts with a TW Barrier Shield and a
magic sword the player picks, three ancient weapons of choice, one weapon for each
W.P. with 1D6+6 spare E-Clips for each (TW weapons with G.M. approval), and any
of the body armors from this book''s equipment section. Armor is not
environmental; some still wear the old horned demon helm for infiltration, while
many prefer a medieval style with angelic wings or plumes.

Magic healing: two White Rose petals per level of experience, two thorns and
two healing potions, with more issued for special missions (the White Rose is
described under the Keeper of the Garden).

Transportation: a horse in M.D.C. barding, and possibly a second, exotic mount
such as a War Bird, Dragon-Cat, Ruin Lizard or Phantom Wolf. Hovercycles,
motorcycles and robot horses are common alternatives.

Money: 1D6x100 credits plus 2D6x1000 credits'' worth of precious metals, gems or
pre-Rifts artifacts. Knights prefer to barter, leaving no money trail.

## GM Notes

The Order numbers about 491 Knights, 662 Squires, 103 Gateways and 138 Keepers,
plus 114 loyal Techno-Wizards, Shifters and Mystics and some 390 civilians in
the Garden. Half the Knights and Squires are away at any time. A Mystic Knight
discovering the Garden would mean an all-out siege.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'knight-of-the-white-rose');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'knight-of-the-white-rose';

